{"wave":{"id":"6155f18a-1b7f-418c-9af3-8d6fa5ce4989","name":"infrastructure","status":"ready","goal":"Loopflow's infrastructure makes ordinary work fast, safe, and boring. It keeps the system legible, converts failures into prevention, and turns repeated operational friction into durable capability.","repo":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow","active_tasks":1,"active_projects":3,"live":true,"paused":false,"enabled":true,"endpoint":"127.0.0.1:57745","created_at":"2026-07-14T18:36:09Z","parent_wave_id":null,"retired_at":null,"superseded_by_wave_id":null,"retirement_reason":null,"home":{"id":"home_39860354aaca640c2ccb50bf6ca609d8","route":"local","created_at":"2026-07-19T14:56:05Z","observed_at":"2026-07-19T14:56:05Z"}},"loop_state":"failed","projects":[{"project":{"id":"03c59a52-dbd4-4e11-a6ac-f6d6359c8e08","slug":"reliability","name":"Reliability","summary":"Maintainers can keep Loopflow advancing its own work and delivering verified releases without repeatedly repairing its coordination machinery. Scheduled delivery reaches truthful, recoverable outcomes; planning and execution remain usable across credentia","definition":"Maintainers can keep Loopflow advancing its own work and delivering verified releases without repeatedly repairing its coordination machinery. Scheduled delivery reaches truthful, recoverable outcomes; planning and execution remain usable across credential expiry, process failure, and upgrades. Recovery preserves work, history, and exact control authority.","flows":{"first":null,"loop":null,"finally":null},"krs":[{"text":"Throughout the chapter, every configured scheduled release opportunity is durably accounted for as on-time, caught up, deferred with a recorded reason and continuation, or failed with an actionable cause. Two consecutive opportunities settle through the configured path as a truthful no-op or complete exact-tag publication; at least one publishes artifacts available to users, all required verification and exact-tag smoke checks pass, and neither settlement requires manual repair. Required scheduled verification failures remain visible and receive an owning repair disposition within one day.","holds":false},{"text":"Across fourteen consecutive days of real Loopflow self-hosting, every attempted core planning or execution operation reaches observable progress, an intentional declared wait, or one bounded, truthful, actionable failure. Ordinary credential expiry with a usable refresh grant does not interrupt planning; recoverable process or controller failures resume without manual state repair. There are no hidden outages, duplicate advancements, lost durable input, terminal-truth regressions, or false availability claims. Recovery preserves assigned-worktree isolation, caller edits, durable history, and exact process authority.","holds":false}]},"runtime":{"work_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-07-21T18:50:07Z","iteration":56,"pending_observations":6,"provider":"codex","last_failure":{"message":"project runner failed: Project plan refresh blocked before the next phase: could not refresh wave/infrastructure from Linear: Stored linear token expired and automatic refresh failed: linear OAuth refresh failed: the token endpoint rejected or could not complete the request. Run `lf auth linear` once to reconnect.. Reconnect or run `lf pm sync --wave infrastructure`.. Project Work proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa did not continue on its stale plan; repair Linear planning, then restart it with `lf project run 03c59a52-dbd4-4e11-a6ac-f6d6359c8e08`","occurred_at":"2026-08-28T22:13:10Z"}},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"tasks":[{"task":{"id":"049348f6-de52-4ac9-a94c-5c0804435668","identifier":"LOO-285","name":"Account for scheduled release opportunities and settle actual release outcomes","description":"The bounded outcome is one authoritative connection between each due opportunity, its execution attempt, verification, and product result. It must distinguish published, no-change, deferred/resumable, and failed outcomes; account for wake delays and overlap without duplication; and demonstrate the two-settlement publication commitment.\n\nUse existing release recovery and obligation-aware continuity code. Do not rebuild the scheduler or create a new release platform. If investigation reveals an independent publication blocker, name that blocker before splitting work. Keep at most one active Reliability implementation Task initially; this is a planning choice, not a runtime restriction.\n\nThe 35 failed telemetry targets remain counterevidence. A successful scheduler firing does not clear them, and required verification cannot be bypassed to obtain a publication receipt.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Queued behind LOO-279 in the same serial Reliability slot. No execution launch or publication occurs as part of creating this planning record.","rank":0,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-285/account-for-scheduled-release-opportunities-and-settle-actual-release","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.125049Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"15172e70-1ec8-4cb0-a15c-f84d49361381","identifier":"LOO-279","name":"Make Linear OAuth recovery survive unattended Project runs","description":"Observed 2026-09-22: Technical Architecture, Performance & Efficiency, and Stability & Security Project runs all stopped before plan refresh because the stored Linear access token expired and automatic refresh was rejected. Restore unattended refresh so headless Project planning continues across token expiry; persist rotated refresh credentials atomically; prove the installed path across expiry and a rejected refresh response; keep reconnect guidance Doppler-aware when user action is genuinely required.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: opening. Finish existing installed-path OAuth recovery; preserve Work, checkout, design and PR identity.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":1,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-279/make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive-unattended-project-runs","workspace":{"slug":"make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive","branch":"jack-heart/make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_81bb835a6bd04748bf99e906aa9f4236","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-09-22T17:35:10Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":{"text":"<lf:steers>\n- Design and ship the smallest fix that makes unattended Linear OAuth refresh reliable for Project plan reads. Start from the three 2026-09-22 Project failures, trace the real installed refresh path, distinguish provider rejection from credential/configuration loss, persist rotated refresh state atomically, and prove expiry plus rejected-refresh behavior through the supported headless path. Preserve fail-closed reconnect guidance and keep it Doppler-aware.\n</lf:steers>"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task has uncommitted work","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.125085Z","evidence_age_secs":81479,"local_progress":{"state":"observed","unsettled":true,"dirty":true,"authored_commits":false,"recovery_required":false,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":"resume","reason":"resume the parked Task"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_4c170525e45e4cbdb9011fcd130aae4d","sequence":1,"slug":"make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive","branch":"jack-heart/make-linear-oauth-recovery-survive","base_commit":"bc80eb6c077e714b8739232491c937759f67271c","phase":"working","empty":false,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_4c170525e45e4cbdb9011fcd130aae4d"},{"task":{"id":"7d5302d8-c861-41f0-8996-5b52312cc2f2","identifier":"LOO-277","name":"Make mutable release worktrees re-enter without losing preparation state","description":"Audit from LOO-259 found a separate restart gap. release_run and finish_release_pr both materialize stable release-<target>-<version> paths through create_named_worktree without holding a path lease. The initial tree is mutated by manifest bumps, repository hooks, and release-note generation before any remote PR head exists; an interruption leaves potentially unique dirty or unpushed bytes that exact-source publisher recovery cannot safely discard. Once an OPEN PR exists, GitHub head_ref_oid is authoritative and reintegration already fetches the exact head, hard-resets to current main, and reruns preparation, but a stale local path or branch makes generic creation fail first. A live release owner also cannot exclude lf wt remove because the lease is acquired only by cleanup.\n\nOutcome: mutable release preparation and reintegration define an evidence-preserving restart policy under an exact path lease. Before a remote PR head exists, preserve unknown dirty or unpushed bytes and report an actionable recovery boundary; never force-remove them. After GitHub supplies an exact PR head, safely converge matching clean partial state into the existing rebuild-from-current-main path, while dirty, divergent, differently registered, and live-owned state remains unchanged. Do not reuse the immutable publisher helper or rebase prepared release artifacts.\n\nProof: production-shaped interruption fixtures cover pre-commit dirty state, post-push clean state, stale branch-only or missing-body registration, dirty or divergent state, and concurrent removal during both initial preparation and reintegration. Exact-head rebuild still reruns every preparation step on current main, and retries neither lose hook output nor publish stale manifests or notes. Start with a scratch design; commit 0683cfe6, PR #1187, and v0.12.6 are the preserved evidence for rebuild-over-rebase.","rank":2,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-277/make-mutable-release-worktrees-re-enter-without-losing-preparation","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185191Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"38644d0a-7a30-4127-8caf-2d76c13db015","identifier":"LOO-273","name":"Make PR landing repair observable and terminating","description":"Make PR landing repair observable and terminating\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:18ed9d63e826489a7c6a68f704954b771aef3706d3e2c81edca369a5f2edc8e6 -->","rank":3,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-273/make-pr-landing-repair-observable-and-terminating","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185194Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"bb8c6014-279a-4028-be3d-e01ea38ceb78","identifier":"LOO-266","name":"Restore caller edits after incomplete release synchronization","description":"Observed 2026-08-22 while resuming v0.12.14 through the scheduled release-run. sync_main auto-stashed overlapping caller edits, including Infrastructure Wave memory. Artifact download then timed out on nightly-x86_64-apple-darwin; the target process exited successfully, publication remained incomplete, and the exact caller memory file was back at its pre-edit content. This is distinct from LOO-259 publisher-worktree ownership and LOO-261 clean-host candidate validation.\\n\\nOutcome: release synchronization never consumes or strands caller worktree changes. Use a dedicated release worktree or a scoped restoration guard so every terminal path—published, resumable failure, transport timeout, or validation failure—returns the caller branch, index, and working bytes exactly as found while preserving tagged release state. A restoration conflict fails with durable, actionable recovery evidence and never silently drops the stash.\\n\\nProof: a release-shaped fixture starts with tracked and untracked caller edits, resumes an existing tag, and injects failure after sync at artifact download and candidate validation. Each exit leaves caller bytes and status identical, retains one resumable release identity, and a later retry publishes once. The success path has the same caller-state guarantee. Start with a scratch design because this changes release recovery ownership.","rank":4,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-266/restore-caller-edits-after-incomplete-release-synchronization","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185195Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"52c7cbaf-0139-4a0e-b1e3-d277f63295ba","identifier":"LOO-262","name":"Read historical CI-incident Runs during local promotion","description":"Read historical CI-incident Runs during local promotion\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:08e05448e16ab4d475dae1ee292d3cb5d7b9fdcd4f776d0fc856169bc9d010e0 -->","rank":5,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-262/read-historical-ci-incident-runs-during-local-promotion","workspace":{"slug":"read-historical-ci-incident-runs","branch":"jack-heart/read-historical-ci-incident-runs","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.read-historical-ci-incident-runs"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_add16f9632ee4253840773d2401abe28","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-23T00:01:14Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-262 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.read-historical-ci-incident-runs is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-262`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185256Z","evidence_age_secs":2736715,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-262 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.read-historical-ci-incident-runs is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-262`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_a842935c5f5543da9f8bc589f9679470","sequence":1,"slug":"read-historical-ci-incident-runs","branch":"jack-heart/read-historical-ci-incident-runs","base_commit":"49b3b403dc8ef6d46ec02390c26b6f82835d04fc","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-22T16:32:55Z","presentation":{"title":"Read historical CI-incident Runs during local promotion — runs: read historical CI incident triggers","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-262](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-262/read-historical-ci-incident-runs-during-local-promotion)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p loopflow ended_run_reads_unknown_trigger_as_byte_exact_historical_evidence\ncargo test -p loopflow installed_development_promotion_reads_arbitrary_historical_run_triggers\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nAllows ended Runs from retired CI controllers to remain readable when their persisted trigger kind is no longer recognized. Unknown triggers are retained as opaque historical evidence with their original JSON unchanged, so development promotion and incident review can consume old Run records without weakening validation for current data.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Parse unknown trigger kinds as historical evidence only for ended Runs\n- Preserve historical trigger JSON byte-for-byte\n- Keep malformed current triggers and unknown nonterminal triggers invalid\n- Validate persisted Run triggers with their Run state during migrations\n- Prevent historical evidence from being used to reserve new Runs","head_sha":"6df87e90ff3c90ca18c1e6fc86be4b9b33be1200"},"github":{"number":1235,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1235"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-22T21:44:25Z","head_sha":"6df87e90ff3c90ca18c1e6fc86be4b9b33be1200","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"a4c73a4c7cc317f9d75a12f583d9bbb1aaee856f","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"c7288e7e-ba26-4a40-81a4-ab9cf4296456","identifier":"LOO-263","name":"Settle merged Task Work atomically from after-merge policy","description":"Observed 2026-08-22 on LOO-226 after PR #1229 merged. The PR record carries `after_merge=complete_task` and Linear is complete, but durable Task Work remains Running with its process alive; the latest durable event is only `pr_merged`, and status recommends a later manual `complete`. A bounded terminal wait did not settle it. Completed LOO-66 corrected impossible action recommendations, not this controller transition.\n\nOutcome: observing the exact merged PR under `after_merge=complete_task` atomically persists the merge fact, terminal Task lifecycle, terminal Work Epoch, Run/Invocation settlement, and exactly one completion event. Process liveness cannot turn the controller-owned transition into an agent follow-up. Reconciliation is idempotent and never mints a synthetic Run.\n\nProof: a production-shaped fixture begins with a live Task Run and an exact merged PR carrying `complete_task`; one reconciliation leaves Task and Work terminal, settles the existing Run/Invocation, records one completion event, and exposes no manual completion action. Repeated reconciliation changes no counts. A stale or non-exact PR cannot settle the Task. Fault injection at event persistence leaves the pre-transition state intact and recoverable. Start with a scratch design because this changes the worker/controller lifecycle boundary.","rank":6,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-263/settle-merged-task-work-atomically-from-after-merge-policy","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185441Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"9a805e26-0dcf-4f69-bad4-d2eeba141df6","identifier":"LOO-265","name":"Make Task promotion recovery depend on live process truth","description":"## Objective\n\nRestore Task availability by making Task-only execution, recovery, and local promotion depend on the current Task Run and direct owned-process observation. Provider invocation, trace, journal, and Exec receipts remain diagnostic metadata and cannot veto that decision.\n\n## Scope\n\n* Remove `prove_absent_run_owners` and both control-path calls. When current Run containment is absent, use the existing cascading recovery to settle the Run and dependent Invocation/Turn state as interrupted or unknown and clear the Task slot.\n* Missing journal context, trace-capture initialization, or later capture writes must not prevent the Task body from running or settling. Preserve a partial-capture warning; remove `trace_capture_blocker` as a non-resumable control outcome.\n* Keep provider resume behavior. Keep exact-owner signaling fail-closed: an unprovable or reused process is never signaled.\n* Limit installed Task promotion to Task/Run process truth. Project/Wave lifecycle adoption and validation are advisory or out of scope for this slice.\n\n## Proof\n\n* An absent Task process with an open Invocation and missing terminal trace or Exec receipts settles and promotion continues.\n* A Task with missing journal context or failed capture initialization/write still executes and settles; status reports partial capture.\n* A foreign, reused, or unprovable live process is never signaled.\n* Existing resume-token behavior remains unchanged.\n* Production-shaped regressions based on LOO-262 and LOO-265 no longer strand a Task on telemetry completeness.\n\n## Not in this slice\n\n* No new supervisor or ProcessOwner schema.\n* No control/trace storage split.\n* No broad liveness or Invocation/Turn type deletion beyond code made dead by this change.\n* No Project/Wave control redesign.\n* No distributed lease or compatibility shim.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:f99d824c429be756188577b2195175f5f7e7cafc2356b490671156c7e7972f4b -->","rank":7,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-265/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-on-live-process-truth","workspace":{"slug":"make-task-promotion-recovery-depend","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-promotion-recovery-depend"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_c185db93945d4a1cb0be74739ad60fd7","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-22T16:33:19Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-265 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-promotion-recovery-depend is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-265`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185472Z","evidence_age_secs":2763590,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-265 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-promotion-recovery-depend is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-265`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_0c573e66dbaa4940800d1eb33b57da8a","sequence":1,"slug":"make-task-promotion-recovery-depend","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend","base_commit":"a4c73a4c7cc317f9d75a12f583d9bbb1aaee856f","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-23T00:01:13Z","presentation":{"title":"Make Task promotion recovery depend on live process truth — Replace Run control plane with decentralized execution records","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-265](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-265/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-on-live-process-truth)","head_sha":"c42743b4a5e41aa27609a8c2ed1cb4365076de06"},"github":{"number":1237,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1237"},"merge":null},"merge_commit":"5f7f66833dafc7cc9e8f1a06cf49f822af0def87","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_7deea05fa0624e5aa7e14c5ebf7863b2","sequence":2,"slug":"2","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-promotion-recovery-depend-2","base_commit":"a72c6c7ff1a36c82a56d113f5adf9b73070fba9f","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_7deea05fa0624e5aa7e14c5ebf7863b2"},{"task":{"id":"3e92e091-4e2b-4b9e-848c-28b741bfcab8","identifier":"LOO-264","name":"Make Home-upgrade promotion retries idempotent","description":"Observed 2026-08-22 while using the supported published refresh from lf 0.12.12 to v0.12.13. Promotion preflight proved the candidate could read 94 persisted lifecycles and safely advance the store, then activation failed with UNIQUE constraint failed: home_upgrade_work.upgrade_id, home_upgrade_work.work_kind, home_upgrade_work.work_id. The installer preserved the 0.12.12 binary and 0.12.12.001_release store frontier. An earlier refused 0.12.14 local promotion had inspected the same active Work set, so a preflight or retry may have left or reused an upgrade identity unexpectedly.\\n\\nOutcome: local and published promotion reserve one exact HomeUpgrade transaction and attach each Work at most once. A refused preflight writes no upgrade rows. Re-entry after any interruption adopts the exact transaction or creates a new non-colliding one, without deleting evidence, bypassing lifecycle checks, or requiring operator database repair.\\n\\nProof: a production-shaped fixture runs a refused candidate preflight followed by a compatible published promotion over the same active Work set; the second promotion completes without a uniqueness error. Repeat at every reservation/attachment interruption boundary and prove one upgrade receipt, one row per Work, unchanged state after refusal, and idempotent same-candidate re-entry. Start with a scratch design because this changes the Home upgrade transaction boundary.","rank":8,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-264/make-home-upgrade-promotion-retries-idempotent","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185645Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"2e903b54-a62e-4e3b-b747-3d1c8e95f7a5","identifier":"LOO-261","name":"Make release candidate validation work from a clean host","description":"Observed 2026-08-21 during the scheduled v0.12.14 release. The release PR merged and the exact tag existed, but final publication failed after artifact download when scripts/publish_release.py ran the downloaded arm64 lf candidate as install preflight --json with LF_CONTROL_DB_PATH pointing at an uninitialized scratch database. The command exited 1, and the wrapper surfaced only CalledProcessError, hiding the candidate diagnostic.\n\nOutcome: release candidate validation succeeds on a clean publisher with no pre-existing Loopflow control database, never opens or mutates the live Home, and preserves the exact candidate failure reason when validation is genuinely unsafe. Adapt the validation context or provide a stateless candidate check; do not weaken install safety or add a live-store bypass.\n\nProof: a release-shaped downloaded artifact passes candidate validation in an empty temporary Home and proceeds to publication; an incompatible candidate fails before publication with a sanitized actionable reason; the live control database remains byte-untouched; same-tag re-entry resumes the tagged v0.12.14 attempt through the publisher-state ownership contract in LOO-259. This is a successor to terminal LOO-215, not a reopening of it.","rank":9,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-261/make-release-candidate-validation-work-from-a-clean-host","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185646Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"52591bd3-0d34-4125-902c-c58ed786386b","identifier":"LOO-255","name":"Tests never touch the live Loopflow home or inherit ambient LF_* state","description":"STANDING QUALITY FRONTIER, not a one-off. Tests must run against their own state — never the live `~/.lf` control-plane DB, and never with ambient `LF_*` / writer-authority env inherited from the Run that launched them. When they leak, the local gate passes but CI (or another machine) fails, and it looks like a flake instead of a missing boundary.\n\nEVIDENCE (recurring):\n\n* #1003 fixed one slice: ambient `LF_*` via EnvGuard's `AMBIENT_TASK_ENV`. Treated as a point fix, so the frontier has no owner.\n* ci-fix on PR #1230 surfaced THREE more in one run: (1) a `git_operation` test saves the ambient writer token but never clears it; (2) a provider-broker test's spawned broker drops `LF_HOME` and reaches the live home; (3) a `wave_context` test opened this Run's live SQLite DB (0.12.13 draft) instead of its fixture.\n\nINTENT — smaller, simpler, and more FLEXIBLE, so we get in our own way less. This is NOT 'lock every test in a rigid sandbox' and NOT more guards/allowlists. The leaks exist because the boundary is rigid in the wrong way: tests assume a fixed ambient home and each one opts out by hand. The fix is to make the system ADAPT to however it's launched — from a live Run, clean CI, or another machine — and resolve the right state for that context automatically, so a test just works wherever it runs. Flexibility over preconditions: fewer hard rules to satisfy, less ambient coupling, a smaller surface where a leak is even possible. Same through-line as 'accept any context, then adapt' (see the main-agents-move-off-canonical work).\n\nPROOF that closes it: the full Rust suite run from inside a live Run/Task Session yields identical results to clean CI, with LESS isolation code than today — per-test scrubbing and the growing `AMBIENT_TASK_ENV` allowlist shrink or disappear because the system adapts to context instead of demanding tests conform to it.\n\nSee memory: cargo-test-inside-task-session.","rank":10,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-255/tests-never-touch-the-live-loopflow-home-or-inherit-ambient-lf-state","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185647Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"1d6723a8-2fe5-465d-b7f5-04586033dbff","identifier":"LOO-243","name":"Carry Run execution context across async Work runners","description":"Observed 2026-08-20 across LOO-226, LOO-229, and LOO-240: each Task runner launches a harness, then records a non-resumable failure because trace_capture_context() finds no active RunContext. The CLI establishes journal::RUN_CONTEXT as thread_local state, while WorkRunner uses Runtime::new().block_on(run_work); Task execution may therefore continue on a Tokio worker thread where the process's context is absent. Project runner currently drops the same missing capture silently. Outcome: pass one explicit, exact Run execution context through Project and Task Work runners across async thread changes; establish it before any provider launch; preserve Run/process identity and authority without inferring from environment or minting a second context; and give Project and Task runners the same fail-closed semantics. Proof: a production-shaped multithreaded __work fixture runs Project and Task bodies with trace capture bound to the supervising Run, records no duplicate Exec/Turn receipts, and demonstrates that a genuinely absent or mismatched context fails before harness launch with an actionable error. This is distinct from LOO-227, which owns durable Project-to-child control Basis.","rank":11,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-243/carry-run-execution-context-across-async-work-runners","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185647Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"815e7193-54b5-4ff3-8d58-020923795e86","identifier":"LOO-240","name":"Restore roadmap and status when persisted Task values are unknown","description":"## Observed failure\n\nOn 2026-08-20, `lf status product --json` exited without a snapshot because one durable row failed validation: `invalid Task: merge request requires reviewer-facing PR copy`. `lf roadmap --json` returned the Wave envelope but marked the entire Project projection unavailable for the same reason. In the same run, `lf pm show --no-sync --json` successfully returned the current three-Project Product snapshot and its Tasks.\n\nCompleted [LOO-202](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-202/expose-one-fleet-snapshot-from-wave-to-raw-trace) established that one stale Project must not erase current Work. Invalid Task validation is a second failure mode at the same product boundary.\n\n## Outcome\n\nFocused status and fleet roadmap remain useful when one durable Task cannot decode. Preserve every valid Wave, Project, Task, Run, and attention row; surface the exact invalid Work as scoped integrity evidence with a legal recovery action. Do not silently coerce the invalid directive, invent defaults, query raw SQLite from clients, or hide the failure.\n\n## Proof\n\nA shared contract fixture contains valid current Work beside one Task whose directive fails validation. `lf status <wave> --json` and `lf roadmap --json` both succeed, retain the valid hierarchy, identify the offending Task and reason, and expose the same recovery semantics. Add a regression test for the exact `merge request requires reviewer-facing PR copy` case.\n\n## Consolidation\n\nThis Task is the sole owner of the invalid persisted-Task resilience fix. It absorbs LOO-233 and duplicate incident placeholder LOO-239. LOO-229 retains the broader current-truth versus historical-state contract; this Task owns degradation of mixed-version or invalid Task rows in roadmap and status readers.","rank":12,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-240/restore-roadmap-and-status-when-persisted-task-values-are-unknown","workspace":{"slug":"restore-roadmap-and-status-when","branch":"jack-heart/restore-roadmap-and-status-when","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-roadmap-and-status-when"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_44a14d08c96e400bb4f5106967bd641e","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-21T17:08:17Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-240 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-roadmap-and-status-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-240`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185676Z","evidence_age_secs":2847892,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-240 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-roadmap-and-status-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-240`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_b0b2ff1458f64579bb6a12ad6d8e2b8a","sequence":1,"slug":"restore-roadmap-and-status-when","branch":"jack-heart/restore-roadmap-and-status-when","base_commit":"631d623667f3dbe8e025cd0585f1ddb7d87d962f","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-21T16:45:54Z","presentation":{"title":"Restore roadmap and status when persisted Task values are unknown — status: preserve released Task PRs without copy","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-240](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-240/restore-roadmap-and-status-when-persisted-task-values-are-unknown)\n\n## Usage\n\n~~~sh\nlf status infrastructure --json\nlf roadmap --wave infrastructure --json\n~~~\n\n## Summary\n\nKeep status and roadmap readable when a released Task PR predates persisted reviewer-facing copy. Persisted-row validation now admits only the historical missing-copy shape, while mutation validation remains strict.\n\n## Changes\n\n- separate persisted-row admission from current Task PR mutation validation\n- add real-binary status and roadmap regressions\n- migrate a frozen 0.12.8 Task PR fixture through the current schema as semantic upgrade proof","head_sha":"fbce236957ebfef468b1d9c16d9ae897d74ad068"},"github":{"number":1219,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1219"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-21T16:45:58Z","head_sha":"fbce236957ebfef468b1d9c16d9ae897d74ad068","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"6de5fd727816426b5171e7ce4fd86e3abf2eb186","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"3a72d757-b396-4af1-83d6-d5b6a8ecda6b","identifier":"LOO-241","name":"Make ledger continuity failures match scheduled obligations","description":"Evidence: the 2026-08-20 telemetry-daily run on release 0.12.10 failed doctor continuity for eight gap days, 2026-08-04 through 2026-08-11, before the telemetry scorecard could run. Existing LOO-219 covers historical capture loss, not cadence continuity.\n\nOutcome: doctor judges continuity against durable scheduler obligations. A day before cadence activation or without an expected run is not silently treated as an outage; a genuinely missed scheduled run names the cron, Home, expected interval, and missing receipt actionably. Unrecoverable historical gaps do not keep every future telemetry run permanently red.\n\nProof: on a copied production-shaped store, explain whether each August 4-11 gap was expected from durable activation and receipt evidence; prove an expected missing day fails with the exact owning cron and Home; prove a pre-activation day is outside the denominator; prove a later successful receipt restores the current window without editing historical observations; and prove telemetry-daily reaches its scorecard once only terminal historical gaps remain.","rank":13,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-241/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-scheduled-obligations","workspace":{"slug":"make-ledger-continuity-failures-match","branch":"jack-heart/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-ledger-continuity-failures-match"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_0bbdf6b9ee424d34ac31d35ee6c7239a","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-28T23:45:04Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-241 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-ledger-continuity-failures-match is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-241`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.185871Z","evidence_age_secs":2219285,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-241 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-ledger-continuity-failures-match is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-241`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_db342829311d4314b38c6e451f7ed5fa","sequence":1,"slug":"make-ledger-continuity-failures-match","branch":"jack-heart/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match","base_commit":"696082a9b1817f192aadfe002ef2252fbc437cb6","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-28T22:31:34Z","presentation":{"title":"LOO-241: Make ledger continuity failures match scheduled obligations","body":"<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [LOO-241 — Make ledger continuity failures match scheduled obligations](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-241/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-scheduled-obligations)\n> **Task cycle:** fix\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## Evaluate\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p loopflow lf::commands::doctor::tests\ncargo test -p loopflow cron\n```\n\nObserve that only a missing scheduled receipt in the latest due interval fails continuity. Historical gaps remain visible, manual receipts do not satisfy the obligation, and a failed scheduled target still proves the scheduler fired. Cron tests also prove unchanged jobs retain activation time and legacy jobs recover it from durable evidence.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nRaw ledger silence was only a proxy for scheduler health, so old gaps could keep daily telemetry red long after service recovered. Comparing installed obligations with scheduled receipts makes failures current, attributable, and actionable without rewriting history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persisted each installed cron's activation timestamp and preserved it across unchanged syncs; changes to its Home, schedule, target, or identity begin a new obligation\n- Recovered legacy activation from the earliest matching scheduled receipt, falling back to the job timestamp\n- Made `lf doctor` evaluate the latest due local-time interval against receipts matching the cron, Home, target kind, schedule, and scheduled source\n- Added actionable failures naming the missing cron, Home, interval, and exact `lf cron history` command\n- Kept pre-activation and older ledger gaps as diagnostic history instead of permanent failures\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\n- Only the latest due interval is enforced; older missed intervals remain historical context by design\n- Continuity proves scheduler execution, not target success; failed targets retain their own receipt and error evidence","head_sha":"7ec881631a3d2342a1cf3f745164e2a6415a9023"},"github":{"number":1248,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1248"},"merge":null},"merge_commit":"b2edd7f5dde31eaa8b1130ebb79b229049ac6ab3","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_7c8484c12a1a4915b22b7070b1a3e140","sequence":2,"slug":"2","branch":"jack-heart/make-ledger-continuity-failures-match-2","base_commit":"b2edd7f5dde31eaa8b1130ebb79b229049ac6ab3","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_7c8484c12a1a4915b22b7070b1a3e140"},{"task":{"id":"9500cecb-4e4a-4c0d-88b1-0186c5ddeb69","identifier":"LOO-226","name":"Install local builds without destroying live work","description":"User outcome\n\nA developer can promote a locally built main or branch through the protected installation transaction used by releases. The first local install uses a disposable clone of the reliable published store; compatible local builds reuse that clone. The installed CLI, daemon, keeper, macOS app, and helpers agree on the selected artifact and Home. A later published release returns to the reliable store without importing dev data. Promotion never destroys live work to make progress.\n\nOne promotion contract\n\n* Route local and published artifacts through one machine-global promotion lock, exact preflight, activation, recovery, keeper restart, and health proof. Never copy or relink installed binaries around that transaction.\n* Keep one reliable published store. A first local install clones it; compatible local installs reuse the dev Home; explicit fresh archives the old dev Home and reclones reliable data. Development binaries never receive reliable-store authority.\n* Treat an exact complete artifact, app/helper, selected-store, migration-frontier, and settled-receipt match as a true no-op before any upgrade receipt, generation change, pause, signal, or reconciliation. Print already installed; fleet untouched.\n* Before a real transition, settle absent owners only from exact Run-event and process-receipt evidence, then classify every live Invocation. Direct provider sessions may stop only with a proved native resume route. Same-lineage headless Work may stop only with a proved lifecycle relaunch. Captured first-fork Work may instead use the confirmed published-return or fresh parking disposition. Any other live or unprovable body defers the entire transition before pause or signal.\n* Preserve typed HomeUpgrade causality. Same-lineage Work relaunches with RunTrigger HomeUpgrade and no retry lineage; confirmed rewind Work stays parked. Neither disposition creates a work-failure event or consumes Task or Project recovery.\n* Use existing provider-session artifacts and command builders to reopen eligible conversations. Link old and replacement Invocations, preserve conversation evidence, and add no second inventory or handoff format.\n* Record exact artifact, store, recovery, first-fork Work, and safe-stop disposition in machine-level promotion authority. Retain the complete published artifact set and reliable store as failback.\n* A published return selects and migrates only the reliable store, parks surviving forked Work before reliable reconciliation, archives the dev Home for inspection, and never imports dev schema or rows.\n\nProof\n\nOne staged integration history proves: an exact reinstall leaves fleet identity untouched; local promotion clones but never mutates the reliable store; a live TUI or ambiguous owner defers promotion without receiving a signal; direct Claude and Codex conversations reopen from existing session artifacts; a headless Task relaunches across same-lineage local upgrades without spending recovery and is durably parked on published return; the 2026-08-19 stale Invocation shape settles exactly once with evidence preserved; keeper and app surfaces retain one artifact/store identity; failure injection leaves valid receipt-owned recovery; and the next published release migrates the reliable store once with no dev-data import.\n\nThis Task absorbs LOO-228 and its 2026-08-19 evidence. Implement one promotion mechanism and preserve the combined acceptance cases in scratch/install-unpublished-local-builds-through.md.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:c4baea4f50bb8eb893840d28ef77483ed740993c3625514fce864cb85b1336a1 -->","rank":14,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-226/install-local-builds-without-destroying-live-work","workspace":{"slug":"install-unpublished-local-builds-through","branch":"jack-heart/install-unpublished-local-builds-through","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.install-unpublished-local-builds-through"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_1b5237f81b7e464db26ba75fad12cdfe","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-22T07:49:38Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-226 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.install-unpublished-local-builds-through is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-226`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.186085Z","evidence_age_secs":2795011,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-226 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.install-unpublished-local-builds-through is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-226`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_177a142ad9654549a99e1616e68599c3","sequence":1,"slug":"install-unpublished-local-builds-through","branch":"jack-heart/install-unpublished-local-builds-through","base_commit":"c06ff52aeefa12aefc28789204916c55065d2576","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-21T20:25:24Z","presentation":{"title":"Install unpublished local builds through the promotion path — install: safely promote unpublished local builds","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-226](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-226/install-local-builds-without-destroying-live-work)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nuv run python scripts/install.py local --use\nuv run python scripts/install.py local --use --fresh\nuv run python scripts/install.py refresh\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nLocal builds can now exercise the installed `lf`, `lfd`, and Loopflow.app surfaces without risking the reliable published Home. Promotion retains the published fallback, forks its data into a disposable development Home, and switches the complete local artifact set through one crash-recoverable drain and relaunch transaction. Refresh returns every surface to the published installation without importing development data.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added machine-scoped install state and entry gates that bind processes to an exact artifact set and store\n- Made CLI, daemon, keeper, app, and active Work transitions recoverable from every persisted switch phase\n- Embedded dependency-ordered draft migrations in development builds and applied only exact append-only prefixes to disposable stores\n- Reused compatible development Homes by default, with `--fresh` available to fork published data again\n- Added end-to-end coverage for promotion, rollback, artifact authorization, Home reuse, and interrupted-switch recovery","head_sha":"df914c1cb8e3bd8dbfddf9f5dc028f9639900ab4"},"github":{"number":1229,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1229"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-22T05:39:53Z","head_sha":"df914c1cb8e3bd8dbfddf9f5dc028f9639900ab4","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"49b3b403dc8ef6d46ec02390c26b6f82835d04fc","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"5f974026-f793-47c1-b499-89f68517a445","identifier":"LOO-224","name":"Wave resident replays stale playhead step names after a skill rename, wedging the loop","description":"Wave resident replays stale playhead step names after a skill rename, wedging the loop\n\nThe product wave (repo /Users/jack/src/loopflow) is stuck loop:failed with '3 consecutive wave failures: failed to prepare wave / wave_mutate: skill not found: wave_mutate'. The catalog registers the skill as wave/mutate (lf list shows it; builtin flow wave.yaml lists wave/clarify -> wave/pursue -> wave/mutate), but the wave's journal playhead pins the pre-rename step name wave_mutate — 5,744 entries in .lf/journal/waves/product/journal.jsonl, replayed across every resident restart including two home upgrades today (2026-08-19). The resident resumes from the persisted playhead instead of re-expanding the flow against the current catalog, so it can never heal. finish_failed_pass fires from run_harness_pass (flowloop/wave.rs:852) when prepare() cannot resolve the stale name.\n\nTask-level flow pins got exactly this repair in #1151 (task runtime: repair stale flow pins and bound recovery); the wave resident needs the same: on prepare failure for a persisted step name, re-expand the flow from the catalog and reconcile the playhead (wave_mutate -> wave/mutate is a rename, index 2 of 3 is unchanged) instead of counting toward consecutive-failure shutdown. Blast radius today: product has 4,317 replays and is wedged; engbot/list have 3 stale refs each; infrastructure 129; all currently idle but will wedge if they resume into a stale pin.\n\nDone when: a wave whose journal pins a renamed step name recovers on the next pass without manual journal surgery (prove with a unit test around the playhead reconciliation, plus the live product wave leaving loop:failed after deploy); consecutive-failure counting distinguishes unresolvable-step (repairable) from body failures.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:a7f376582cd1bb7bd0b467dcae85e593f9d5139e995e5cfa7bf715287e37d468 -->","rank":15,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-224/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead-step-names-after-a-skill-rename","workspace":{"slug":"wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead","branch":"jack-heart/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_1c8661873b4a4f8f97a4e4234b555701","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-28T22:22:00Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-224 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-224`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.186259Z","evidence_age_secs":2224269,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-224 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-224`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_44069c31243049e7b8a0742c1f8db6f0","sequence":1,"slug":"wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead","branch":"jack-heart/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead","base_commit":"bcea828c8bd29fe40c1365720c0938a7e2459acd","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-20T01:04:06Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1202,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1202"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-20T08:48:32Z","head_sha":"741c20dd65580de19b76dabd6ac9f1a2ad7cbf5d","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"a124f821204353587c4667e1c60f016f02251e7d","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_93427b1823be4a73be1498e6dcfefddb","sequence":2,"slug":"2","branch":"jack-heart/wave-resident-replays-stale-playhead-2","base_commit":"a124f821204353587c4667e1c60f016f02251e7d","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_93427b1823be4a73be1498e6dcfefddb"},{"task":{"id":"17edc7a0-5e01-444a-8c6b-ccaf2ead7250","identifier":"LOO-228","name":"[absorbed] Home upgrades must not destroy work they cannot resume","description":"Absorbed into LOO-226. The survivor now contains the committed 2026-08-19 incident evidence, exact reinstall no-op, fail-closed pre-signal liveness classification, typed HomeUpgrade causality outside the Work recovery budget, exact dead-owner settlement, provider-session continuity, and the combined local-promotion proof. The older leave-unresumable-processes-behind proposal is resolved to deferral before pause or signal. Do not implement this Task independently.","rank":16,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-228/absorbed-home-upgrades-must-not-destroy-work-they-cannot-resume","workspace":{"slug":"home-upgrades-must-not-destroy","branch":"jack-heart/home-upgrades-must-not-destroy","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.home-upgrades-must-not-destroy"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_d1a5666cb9564576b3944f2bbf5ef67a","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-21T02:02:16Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-228 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.home-upgrades-must-not-destroy is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/home-upgrades-must-not-destroy\" before `lf task resume LOO-228`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.186455Z","evidence_age_secs":2902253,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-228 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.home-upgrades-must-not-destroy is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/home-upgrades-must-not-destroy\" before `lf task resume LOO-228`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_c8fe8ff17f7b4fa08c35d539569f1604","sequence":1,"slug":"home-upgrades-must-not-destroy","branch":"jack-heart/home-upgrades-must-not-destroy","base_commit":"dd8eca9815a860fa69c573cadbe3d5ae9c9c912e","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_c8fe8ff17f7b4fa08c35d539569f1604"},{"task":{"id":"cf5f19cd-731b-4f5d-81c4-989eaaa00a20","identifier":"LOO-229","name":"Status surfaces must distinguish last recorded event from current truth","description":"Status surfaces must distinguish last recorded event from current truth\n\nEvidence from 2026-08-19, three instances of one defect: (1) lf status showed 'project runner failed: no eligible managed codex account ... credential is missing' for every infrastructure project all day, replaying terminal project_events from Jul 22 / Aug 14 — the account store had been healthy since Aug 16 and concurrent runners were selecting accounts fine; (2) wave headers showed loop:failed replayed from journals across restarts even while every project and task under the wave ran normally; (3) agent_invocations kept invocation_74115449 as outcome='running' for hours after its process died in an upgrade, and lf invocation status could not resolve the id it was still reporting as live.\n\nScope: every read surface (lf status, lf ls, invocation list, Mac app equivalents) must either verify a claimed-live fact against liveness evidence or label it as historical ('last failure at <time>', not 'failed'). Startup/reconcile should settle records whose backing process provably did not return, in the spirit of #1151 and LOO-224 but as a general rule for run/invocation records rather than a per-noun patch. Stale-state incidents today all shared the shape: durable record outlives reality and is replayed as present tense.\n\nDone when: a terminal failure record older than the newest successful run of the same work renders as history, not as the current state (fixture-level proof plus one live lf status demo); an invocation whose process is gone is settled by reconcile within one startup cycle; the Jul-22 credential ghost cannot recur — reproduce it in a test store and show the new rendering.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:39d177a93bf486c5cbd6820097b6836af50dd4f75a9355c34ffe4dc0dd381fbe -->\n\n## Ownership boundary — 2026-08-20\n\nLOO-240 owns degradation when one persisted Task row cannot decode, including the exact `merge request requires reviewer-facing PR copy` fixture. This Task retains the broader contract: status surfaces must distinguish historical records from current liveness and reconcile exact dead owners. Depend on LOO-240 for mixed-version row availability; do not implement a second partial-reader path here.","rank":17,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-229/status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last-recorded-event-from-current","workspace":{"slug":"status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last","branch":"jack-heart/status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9afb8feb2e1840728e066f9c1ea5e2a7","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-21T22:26:52Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-229 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-229`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.186587Z","evidence_age_secs":2828777,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-229 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-229`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_d7f75974b74a401bb197c4e209d2c4e3","sequence":1,"slug":"status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last","branch":"jack-heart/status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last","base_commit":"ab39cb83df0e8313e54300fa64fde2b950e14574","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-21T19:56:39Z","presentation":{"title":"Status surfaces must distinguish last recorded event from current truth — status: separate current work truth from history","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-229](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-229/status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last-recorded-event-from-current)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf status <wave>\nlf status <wave> --json\nlf invocation list --active\n```\n\nStatus now reports current Work as `working`, `stalled`, `stopped`, or `unobservable` from fresh Home-owned evidence. Earlier failures remain separately labeled as `last failure`, and invocations without verified liveness appear as `unverified` rather than running.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR prevents historical events and stale process records from impersonating current state across the CLI, roadmap, Context Lab, and Mac app. The owning Home records tri-state Run liveness and reconciles active Runs, giving every status surface one shared projection of what is true now while preserving failures and retired Work as explicit history.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a shared `CurrentWorkObservation` model for Wave, Project, and Task state, ownership, controls, progress, and liveness evidence\n- Added bounded `present`, `absent`, and `unprovable` containment probes plus startup and periodic `lfd` reconciliation for nonterminal Runs and stranded Asks\n- Moved Project failures into timestamped `last_failure` history with Run attribution where it can be proven\n- Require fresh Home evidence before capture-ledger invocations are presented as running; otherwise surface them as unverified\n- Preserve retired Wave identities during locator replacement and keep unavailable Projects and orphaned Tasks visible in status and roadmap output\n- Updated the SQLite migration, Rust/Swift DTO fixtures, CLI rendering, Mac views, and focused behavioral coverage\n\n## Compatibility\n\nThe status DTOs replace the previous body/process fields with required current-state and liveness fields. Rust producers and Swift consumers are updated together; external JSON consumers must migrate to the new shape.","head_sha":"db2832c40be4ade34465ab0d00002cf6aac6b061"},"github":{"number":1225,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1225"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-21T22:12:30Z","head_sha":"db2832c40be4ade34465ab0d00002cf6aac6b061","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"521ae7d3f01f1e46618ab2247ffccdf3f41411d2","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"db77bbf0-2ea0-4c47-9512-3fda3a963f34","identifier":"LOO-227","name":"Let Project runs resume child Tasks with durable control authority","description":"Observed 2026-08-19 in Stability & Security iteration 36: the authoritative roadmap recommended resuming parked LOO-224, but `lf task resume LOO-224 --json` failed closed before mutation with `invalid control authority: Run run_8ee1a67cc30a4bc9b70905b92cb0d68d has no durable Turn Basis for child control`. LOO-224 retained its worktree, passing PR #1202, and unresolved wait; no duplicate Run was created. User outcome: every Project phase permitted to supervise child Tasks carries durable, exact control authority across phase transitions and provider/process recovery, so a recommended resume cannot strand the Task. Done when a real Project/pursue Run can resume an existing parked child Task; the authority is bound to the exact Project Work and Turn Basis; a retry is idempotent; an unrelated Project or stale Turn remains denied; and a missing basis surfaces as actionable Project failure before pursuit rather than leaving the child parked. Add a deterministic behavior fixture for phase transition plus process-loss recovery. Do not weaken task authority or bypass the existing resume path.","rank":18,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-227/let-project-runs-resume-child-tasks-with-durable-control-authority","workspace":{"slug":"let-project-runs-resume-child","branch":"jack-heart/let-project-runs-resume-child","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-project-runs-resume-child"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9a1fadffa162496392fad774d290b427","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-28T23:55:40Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-227 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-project-runs-resume-child is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/let-project-runs-resume-child\" before `lf task resume LOO-227`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.18673Z","evidence_age_secs":2218649,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-227 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-project-runs-resume-child is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/let-project-runs-resume-child\" before `lf task resume LOO-227`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_4eb3598612a44d18b677590a525301be","sequence":1,"slug":"let-project-runs-resume-child","branch":"jack-heart/let-project-runs-resume-child","base_commit":"a72c6c7ff1a36c82a56d113f5adf9b73070fba9f","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":"pr_4eb3598612a44d18b677590a525301be"},{"task":{"id":"aad2d373-8f99-41e5-9ddf-79996266fceb","identifier":"LOO-219","name":"Keep daily telemetry actionable after historical capture loss","description":"Observed 2026-07-21: the due telemetry-daily flow failed because lf doctor reports 20,703 partial capture records. Representative provider and conversation traces record No space left on device on 2026-07-14 and 2026-07-15. Current evidence contradicts an active capacity outage: the Home volume has 169 GiB available, .lf/traces uses 11 GiB, and .lf uses 23 GiB. Outcome: preserve historical partial-capture facts while letting telemetry distinguish recovered current health from new active loss. Done when historical partials remain visible and immutable; a healthy post-recovery window can pass; any new capture loss fails immediately with time, owner, and storage context; text and JSON doctor output agree; deterministic fixtures cover historical loss plus current health and a newly recurring failure. Do not delete or rewrite trace history, add an unbounded ignore list, or weaken release verification.","rank":19,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-219/keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after-historical-capture-loss","workspace":{"slug":"keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after","branch":"jack-heart/keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9b75352d38194438af022bd739cae8d0","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-22T20:27:08Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-219 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-219`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.186902Z","evidence_age_secs":5427961,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-219 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-219`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_7c67e2f96a6d4347a6c1e718c347d0ce","sequence":1,"slug":"keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after","branch":"jack-heart/keep-daily-telemetry-actionable-after","base_commit":"7dbca69d082babcd3cd495942b3c56629e04b301","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T18:21:33Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1178,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1178"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T20:05:21Z","head_sha":"83d3a88547227946a8d841fe522ea5a20270c524","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"90b89225c240b84fc77d40a2ec99c2d8b3b3acae","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"776e020e-c2e6-4b3c-b320-802494c59ce1","identifier":"LOO-17","name":"[subsumed by LOO-102] Make the development Mac app use the shared registry safely","description":"scripts/loopflow-dev.py run and run-debug currently bundle a development-provenance lf, which defaults to an empty per-worktree database. The app launches successfully but cannot see the real Waves, Tasks, or interactive handoffs it is supposed to demo. Build the bundled demo CLI from the current checkout with release store selection and validation-only migration authority, so it reads the shared registry without gaining permission to migrate it. Prove the installed Dev app bundled lf ls --json matches the installed CLI Wave identities and that run-debug still refuses any required production migration.","rank":20,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-17/subsumed-by-loo-102-make-the-development-mac-app-use-the-shared","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187048Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"c794339e-4e49-48d1-ab82-7322d78c9f6d","identifier":"LOO-214","name":"Bootstrap the infrastructure cron host and its durable receipts","description":"Install the infrastructure Wave's declared telemetry-daily and release-run jobs on its placed Home using the supported lf cron path. Preflight host-local/Doppler authority without exposing secrets. Prove lf cron list matches GOAL.md, each flow can run through the configured path, and scheduled success/failure leaves durable, actionable evidence sufficient to start the nightly/weekly and host-drift observation windows. Do not build a generic deployment platform or alter completed Task work.","rank":21,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-214/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-and-its-durable-receipts","workspace":{"slug":"bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-5","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_0c8bdce62d594ff9ab08e5a3553e294d","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-16T20:54:57Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-214 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-214`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187078Z","evidence_age_secs":3266292,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-214 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-214`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_f0692a39cd074b90b0ca2d2481f206a7","sequence":1,"slug":"bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host","base_commit":"026dc10c7357edc7f636cfc589e2ddc9bfc7fb0f","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T22:41:57Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1171,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1171"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T17:50:17Z","head_sha":"d037b3c816c6b4a8b6209edfe65f0e6c7eb5744c","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":"installed-cron-proof"}},"merge_commit":"553a6e3806a56e9c31c6cb94566de5aad352bf42","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_7a422374904e4d4d8d5a1c1751f51c9c","sequence":2,"slug":"installed-cron-proof","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-installed-cron-proof","base_commit":"3d1034c771ea36a5f670eff69a6a45ba94f267b2","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T18:22:08Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1179,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1179"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T18:28:29Z","head_sha":"efe9562858b774eb35039b365a28ebf31d7a13bc","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"ae38c2049d6493498150832d72b957e6d9ea194a","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_78c73ce267a947c381d506dfa8e679cd","sequence":3,"slug":"3","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-3","base_commit":"9e5736a90c7946e3abfbe44742ffc466b5808ef2","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T18:59:28Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1181,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1181"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T19:09:42Z","head_sha":"7e3d8fafb632ad5a56b6014b6124580f7a5d2ab5","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"7dbca69d082babcd3cd495942b3c56629e04b301","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_8f20fb7e3d0c408ea3562477f1f6014d","sequence":4,"slug":"4","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-4","base_commit":"7dbca69d082babcd3cd495942b3c56629e04b301","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T20:11:48Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1183,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1183"},"merge":null},"merge_commit":"6d9aef3d2d4488cadf1cae4a2aa86bff6d192949","abandoned_at":null},{"id":"pr_ded3de37bc1b4056a83a290c4d7a91da","sequence":5,"slug":"5","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-infrastructure-cron-host-5","base_commit":"e23ba5842cbb29d66c727232b1e545b66d7157a3","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T23:12:32Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1187,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1187"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T23:24:38Z","head_sha":"4f7abf23b2cf512a79937740c3558b2f088f01cb","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"0683cfe6cb4b56322aa4edb069116f6ccf5d9388","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"ae4775c7-a2a6-4a91-a3f3-65153dae363a","identifier":"LOO-29","name":"[subsumed by LOO-55] Report the authoritative PR base without false contamination","description":"Found by W2-306 while diagnosing the re-mint base incoherence, and correctly left out of its scope. Filed by the Project because a Task session does not file its own follow-ups.\n\n## The defect\n\nops/task.rs:1497-1511 classifies merge_base < base as:\n\n'PR range is contaminated: recorded base carries commit(s) not on origin/main'\n\nThat is the #877/#882 foreign-ancestry case. It is FALSE for the mint bug. W2-300's row hits this arm — is_ancestor(9f6bdd498, 3e9df0677) is true — yet base 3e9df0677 IS origin/main's tip and carries nothing foreign. The message accuses the base of exactly the property it does not have, which sends a reader hunting foreign ancestry that is not there.\n\nThe arm conflates two distinct causes:\n\n* (a) base is ON the upstream but AHEAD of the branch's fork point — the mint bug W2-306 fixes;\n* (b) base is OFF the upstream carrying foreign commits — genuine contamination (#877/#882).\n\nis_ancestor(base, upstream) separates them cleanly: true => (a), false => (b).\n\n## Why this survives W2-306\n\nW2-306 makes cause (a) unrepresentable going forward at the mint, and heals existing rows on adopt. So after it lands this message should become unreachable for (a) — but 'unreachable' is an assumption worth testing, not a reason to leave a lying diagnostic in the tree. Any future path that records a base ahead of the fork point lands here again and gets misdiagnosed.\n\n## Done when\n\n* The M<B arm distinguishes (a) from (b) via is_ancestor(base, upstream) and each names its real cause. A base that is the upstream's own tip must never be described as carrying commits not on the upstream.\n* A test pins each arm separately with a fixture that actually has the property the message asserts. A single test over one shape passes with the conflation fully present — this is the same trap that hid the mint bug (a first-mint-only test is green while the defect is live).\n* Do NOT change the fail-closed behaviour; only the classification and the text. Both arms still refuse.\n\n## Context\n\nDepends on nothing; W2-306 (#1059) may land first and is expected to. Read W2-306's design (scratch/a-re-minted-successor-pairs.md) for the base/merge_base model before touching this: base_commit == merge_base(upstream, branch) is the invariant the tree already states at ops/task.rs:1492 and 3455-3458.","rank":22,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-29/subsumed-by-loo-55-report-the-authoritative-pr-base-without-false","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187303Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"9ddb3775-2ea0-40c1-b88c-c7ac623c6dd5","identifier":"LOO-32","name":"[subsumed by LOO-37] Bound release notes and release-queue metadata","description":"Observed while recovering the v0.11.3 release on 2026-07-15. The deterministic notes fallback generated a 140,834-byte RELEASE_NOTES.md by copying full historical PR bodies. `lf release run patch` then passed that entire document as the squash commit body, and GitHub rejected auto-merge at its 16,383-character commit-message limit.\\n\\nUser story\\n\\nAs the release operator, deterministic fallback notes stay reviewable and the release PR can always enter the merge queue regardless of historical PR-body size.\\n\\nDone when\\n\\n- The PR set is exactly the commits after the previous release tag; already-released history is excluded.\\n- Mechanical notes summarize or omit PR bodies under an explicit documented byte budget.\\n- PR presentation and squash commit metadata have separate bounded copy.\\n- A fixture with many very large PR bodies produces useful notes and successfully reaches the queue call.\\n- Truncation is visible and deterministic, never silent corruption.\\n\\nSource: release PR #987 and W2-257. Recovery manually reduced the v0.11.3 PR body from about 140 KB to 2.1 KB.","rank":23,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-32/subsumed-by-loo-37-bound-release-notes-and-release-queue-metadata","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187304Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"7572c986-583a-4876-878d-6c3d491980fb","identifier":"LOO-212","name":"Bootstrap the release Home's Doppler authority","description":"Restore patch-release readiness after the 2026-07-21 release-run failed before mutation. Evidence: doppler run -- uv run python scripts/publish_release.py check reported missing secret names CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN, FLY_API_TOKEN, NOTARY_ISSUER, NOTARY_KEY, NOTARY_KEY_ID, R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID, R2_ACCOUNT_ID, and R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY on Home home_39860354aaca640c2ccb50bf6ca609d8. Inspect Home placement and the configured Doppler project/config without printing values. If values require new human authority, create one durable Ask naming the exact destination and secret names. Otherwise repair configuration. Done when the same check exits zero. Do not publish a release as part of this Task.","rank":24,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-212/bootstrap-the-release-homes-doppler-authority","workspace":{"slug":"bootstrap-the-release-home-s","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-release-home-s","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-release-home-s"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_3c342ae78ac6462cada4df59da63b77b","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:29:23Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-212 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-release-home-s is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-212`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187326Z","evidence_age_secs":5510626,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-212 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.bootstrap-the-release-home-s is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-212`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_4e48b9c53d784e8a87bffde86ffdf104","sequence":1,"slug":"bootstrap-the-release-home-s","branch":"jack-heart/bootstrap-the-release-home-s","base_commit":"a8bcc90585fac0cb0d7d0b627488a702a64aefb4","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T21:00:33Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1164,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1164"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:12Z","head_sha":"4c756eef93b6a6b6dbe86b439be72fd96cbf4a98","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"07e1902bf6a2e49c0cd0551610a8ee62b012a602","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"7150136b-c614-4ea4-8a0d-f89d45a8ffd6","identifier":"LOO-37","name":"Make releases finish predictably when automation is degraded","description":"Outcome: A release remains bounded, useful, and safely resumable when the notes agent is unavailable, rate-limited, unauthenticated, or otherwise degraded. Contract: mechanical release context and queue metadata have explicit size bounds; agent notes use bounded source material; every provider unavailability class selects the supported deterministic fallback; retries neither duplicate release state nor grow context without bound; status distinguishes degraded notes from an unsafe release gate. Proof: tests cover missing CLI, cooldown, quota, authentication failure, oversized PR bodies, interrupted retry, and a successful resumed release that produces concise notes and the exact intended artifact once.","rank":25,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-37/make-releases-finish-predictably-when-automation-is-degraded","workspace":{"slug":"make-releases-finish-predictably-when","branch":"jack-heart/make-releases-finish-predictably-when","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-releases-finish-predictably-when"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_a6b589abc8d74427b1fefbac74f17937","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T20:05:11Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-37 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-releases-finish-predictably-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-37`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187547Z","evidence_age_secs":5515678,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-37 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-releases-finish-predictably-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-37`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_8a5cb56f41304e4e88472e14e6461746","sequence":1,"slug":"make-releases-finish-predictably-when","branch":"jack-heart/make-releases-finish-predictably-when","base_commit":"4fa8d8b5777a700b64e950e9de82233761cd6e9d","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T19:21:31Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1158,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1158"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T19:53:32Z","head_sha":"74f1376302c7ff52227e057240fe0f4c6e0e0c2b","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"ebb858a9f22aae15484675ed1e10514cd1520977","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"998ea80e-790c-4039-b7b8-5555af56159c","identifier":"LOO-39","name":"[subsumed by LOO-102] Synchronize Wave wakes on events","description":"Observed in merge-group CI for migration PR #986 on 2026-07-15. The ordinary PR run and the full local `cargo test -p loopflow` passed, but merge-group rust-test failed `flowloop::wave::tests::say_wakes_the_loop_and_is_consumed_by_the_next_pass` after 3.137s with `condition not met in time: pass spawned`; 552 tests had passed and the remaining suite was canceled. The same test passed in the prior runs.\n\nUser-visible outcome\n\nWave runtime tests prove wake/consume ordering deterministically under loaded CI. They wait on an owned event or state transition, not a three-second scheduling race, and a real failure still reports which transition never occurred.\n\nProof\n\nReproduce the failure under parallel nextest load, replace wall-clock polling with deterministic synchronization at the runtime boundary, and run the test repeatedly plus the full nextest profile. Follow the repository rule: do not add retries or merely extend the timeout; delete a test if it cannot prove user behavior deterministically.","rank":26,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-39/subsumed-by-loo-102-synchronize-wave-wakes-on-events","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187686Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"910993d2-0c1e-4b34-b8cd-2343d9109854","identifier":"LOO-55","name":"Let a Task ship without corrupting neighboring work or needing manual repair","description":"Outcome: A Task can move from launch to merged PR without writing outside its assignment, leaving provider processes behind, falsely rejecting its own branch, or requiring a human to reconstruct CI state. Contract: one writer owns the assigned worktree and provider write tools cannot modify main or another Task even when those paths are readable; normal exit reaps provider descendants and lfd maintenance reaps only registry-proven orphans; PR range diagnostics use the authoritative upstream base and never call origin main foreign contamination; one bounded ci-fix turn owns repair of the authoritative failed head and settles truthfully. Proof: an end-to-end lifecycle covers worktree escape attempts, provider exit and forced orphan recovery, rebased publication, failed CI repair, and terminal settlement with zero manual Git or process cleanup.","rank":27,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-55/let-a-task-ship-without-corrupting-neighboring-work-or-needing-manual","workspace":{"slug":"let-a-task-ship-without","branch":"jack-heart/let-a-task-ship-without","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-a-task-ship-without"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_cb620426f83c40a583bdd1bea22a0b99","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:11:39Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-55 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-a-task-ship-without is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-55`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187707Z","evidence_age_secs":5511690,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-55 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-a-task-ship-without is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-55`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_fe0a71fb7f79478390248db5c6f7865b","sequence":1,"slug":"let-a-task-ship-without","branch":"jack-heart/let-a-task-ship-without","base_commit":"cc3f7a44fb54f3bbc1f9e17b478c38a57667379f","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T20:20:08Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1163,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1163"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T20:58:24Z","head_sha":"9b836e8a4cc08335837595b02833d5fcbdd3bbf2","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"62bcab9b8baa63937a6983523d3f1e0b4d3815d3","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"5efbfd37-8d3a-417d-8e20-d8f2fc59e3df","identifier":"LOO-57","name":"Keep Wave status readable when a historical Project leaves the PM snapshot","description":"Reproduced on 2026-07-15 after `lf pm show --wave infrastructure --sync` succeeded. Both `lf roadmap --wave infrastructure --json` and `lf status infrastructure --json` still fail because historical Project Session `release-stability` (6c053501-f727-42cf-a1a3-8fc788e82410) is present in the registry but absent from the current Linear PM snapshot. This was previously reported during the migration fire and remains red.\n\nUser-visible outcome\n\nWave status always renders current work even when the durable registry contains Sessions for a renamed, retired, archived, or otherwise absent Project. Historical work remains visible as historical/degraded evidence and cannot make the entire Wave map unavailable.\n\nProof\n\nCreate a registry with current Tasks plus a historical Project Session omitted from the PM snapshot. `lf status` and `lf roadmap` must render current projects, classify the orphaned historical session explicitly, and give an actionable reconciliation owner. Preserve history; do not delete the Session or synthesize a fake PM project.","rank":28,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-57/keep-wave-status-readable-when-a-historical-project-leaves-the-pm","workspace":{"slug":"keep-wave-status-readable-when","branch":"jack-heart/keep-wave-status-readable-when","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-wave-status-readable-when"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_a1477e45045d4a7baac72c0d9b862de6","project_id":"proj_d28ac50d38f376165b4af5b696ff11eb","routing_project_id":"proj_d28ac50d38f376165b4af5b696ff11eb","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T18:49:10Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-57 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-wave-status-readable-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-57`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.187869Z","evidence_age_secs":5520239,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-57 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-wave-status-readable-when is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-57`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_0a3b6d9ea82940e0ad6bb0a1e62db8a7","sequence":1,"slug":"keep-wave-status-readable-when","branch":"jack-heart/keep-wave-status-readable-when","base_commit":"823e12d5e7426cd6550c8d4e8a6e04470d315cda","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T18:35:47Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1152,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1152"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T18:35:51Z","head_sha":"e11c68494c3d5401db00ce4e8a81842918512167","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"38b40660736d6aeb39d29a0a4617b0bb00853c93","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"9e3c71ba-78aa-4da2-986a-bef5c0130409","identifier":"LOO-62","name":"[subsumed by LOO-55] Reap provider subprocesses when a body exits","description":"Observed on 2026-07-15 after W2-225 generation 10 failed because its historical lf binary disappeared. The lf Task body and tmux session exited, but an orphaned `opencode serve` process remained under PPID 1 in the Task worktree for more than 90 minutes. `lf top` still reported it even though `lf task status W2-225` correctly said no process was alive.\n\nUser-visible outcome\n\nWhen a Project or Task body completes, fails, is interrupted, or disappears, every provider subprocess it owns is terminated within a bounded grace period. A provider must not outlive its durable body lease, retain ports, or make a dead worktree look occupied. Cleanup must target the owned process group and never kill unrelated provider sessions.\n\nProof\n\nCover normal completion, wrapper failure before terminal outcome, interrupt, and lost-body reconciliation. Start a provider child, terminate the body, and prove the child/process group is reaped while an unrelated provider stays alive. `lf top` and Task status must agree after cleanup.","rank":29,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-62/subsumed-by-loo-55-reap-provider-subprocesses-when-a-body-exits","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188016Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"fe0b2e61-7a11-4ddc-a627-bbed371bc921","identifier":"LOO-102","name":"Make every Wave start and wake reliably from supported surfaces","description":"Outcome: A Wave starts from the CLI, development Mac app, or a fresh Home and becomes responsive without registry confusion, partial registration, or polling-dependent luck. Contract: first start either publishes a live lfd endpoint or rolls back and names the actionable failure; the Mac app and CLI use the intended shared registry without replacing a promoted binary unsafely; wake behavior synchronizes on durable events rather than wall-clock sleeps; one Wave startup failure does not kill unrelated Home work. Proof: end-to-end tests cover fresh Home, installed lfd, development app, already-registered Wave, concurrent wake, and failed preflight, and every path reaches a truthful live or failed state within a bounded interval.","rank":30,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-102/make-every-wave-start-and-wake-reliably-from-supported-surfaces","workspace":{"slug":"make-every-wave-start-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-every-wave-start-and","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-wave-start-and"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_a8556ddc65b9483cb7e3bb1b3b56a027","project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","routing_project_id":"proj_33676884d672454780209ce4e5b624fa","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T20:48:16Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-102 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-wave-start-and is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-102`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188039Z","evidence_age_secs":5513093,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-102 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-wave-start-and is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-102`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_cacc9a1713d4455492f5697474734459","sequence":1,"slug":"make-every-wave-start-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-every-wave-start-and","base_commit":"649121be5435926ae44a398fd4ba3e21fb44d5c5","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T20:04:26Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1161,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1161"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T20:35:57Z","head_sha":"5c3c247ba37387207ab5e7909b67927da4e2e7ac","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"cc3f7a44fb54f3bbc1f9e17b478c38a57667379f","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"3cc1493f-a29f-4f9d-80b8-fb378340ba9d","identifier":"LOO-104","name":"[subsumed by LOO-55] Reap registry-proven orphan providers from lfd maintenance","description":"Extend lfd's startup and fifteen-minute Home maintenance sweep to terminate provider process groups whose exact Loopflow owner registry entry points to an absent owner. Send TERM, wait a bounded grace, then KILL the verified group and persist a reap receipt. Never terminate stalled, unobservable, PID-reused, or merely unclaimed processes. This complements the existing exit-time provider-subprocess cleanup task: exit cleanup is the normal path; lfd is the crash/reboot recovery path. Done when a registered orphan disappears without a Wave restart, a live owner vetoes reaping, repeated sweeps are idempotent, and lf top can explain the recent cleanup from its receipt.","rank":31,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-104/subsumed-by-loo-55-reap-registry-proven-orphan-providers-from-lfd","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188163Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"761827cc-cee7-4a77-9e93-3bfef6825535","identifier":"LOO-105","name":"[subsumed by LOO-55] Prove deterministic ci-fix recovery on the Run spine","description":"## Context\n\nPRD-8 (product wave, \"Wake a waiting Task into ci-fix when its PR fails\") depends on four Infrastructure substrate tasks whose merged evidence was meant to satisfy its done-whens. All four are marked done in Linear:\n\n* ENG-88 / W2-229 — Prove failed-PR ci-fix recovery as one deterministic lifecycle (#1009)\n* ENG-20 / W2-230 — Route automatic ci-fix wakes through the durable Task command ledger (#1024)\n* ENG-87 / W2-231 — Make ci-fix infrastructure failures block the Task actionably (#1001)\n* ENG-19 / W2-232 — Settle one bounded ci-fix turn without entering the generic Task gate (#1063)\n\n## The gap (found 2026-07-18 while auditing PRD-8 directive v4)\n\nThe architecture refactor #1073 (\"establish the durable Run and Steer control spine\") swept away two of the four implementations AFTER they merged:\n\n* ENG-88's 2817-line deterministic lifecycle harness (`rust/loopflow/src/task/runner/ci_fix_lifecycle_tests.rs`) was **deleted** in #1073 and **not replaced**. Current ci-fix test coverage on main is only unit tests: `ci_fix_restart_bar_permits_only_a_failing_open_pr_wake` (1), `merge_gate*` (3), and `autonomy*` (4). No test exercises the full wake → fix → green → rearm path deterministically.\n* ENG-20's durable command ledger (`ChildCommand` aggregate + `queue_command`) was **deleted** in #1073 via migration `0.11.035_drop_child_commands.sql`. The wake is now recorded through the `ci_incidents` store (`claim_ci_incident`, `mark_ci_incident_repaired`, `mark_ci_incidents_blocked`) on the Run/Launch/Basis spine. Whether that satisfies the \"durable audited ci-fix command ledger\" done-when needs a deliberate decision, not a silent replacement.\n\nENG-87 (blocked semantics) and ENG-19 (bounded settlement) survive in refactored form (`settle_ci_fix_turn`, `mark_ci_incidents_blocked` in `rust/loopflow/src/task/runner.rs`).\n\n## What this task owns\n\nRe-establish the deterministic lifecycle proof on the current Run/Launch/Basis architecture so PRD-8's original done-when #1 holds again:\n\n> A deterministic integration harness opens a PR and proves: pending checks consume no body; one required failure starts exactly one ci-fix turn with canonical metadata; duplicate and multi-check deliveries coalesce; the fix pushes the same branch/PR and rearms observation for the new SHA; green CI does not wake a body; and an infrastructure failure produces an actionable blocker without code churn.\n\nAnd confirm whether the `ci_incidents` store on the Run spine satisfies ENG-20's \"durable audited command ledger\" intent, or whether a dedicated audit record is still warranted.\n\n## What this task does NOT own\n\nThe ci-fix wake mechanism itself (PR 967, product) and the blocked-semantics / bounded-settlement behavior (ENG-87, ENG-19). This is proof-and-audit restoration only, on the architecture that replaced the originals.\n\n## Why PRD-8 stays open\n\nPRD-8 directive v4 says: keep PRD-8 open and visibly dependent on the Infrastructure tasks until their merged evidence satisfies the original done-whens. The merged evidence no longer satisfies them because #1073 removed the proof. PRD-8 cannot close until this task (or equivalent proof) lands.","rank":32,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-105/subsumed-by-loo-55-prove-deterministic-ci-fix-recovery-on-the-run","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188163Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null}]},{"project":{"id":"62b73cde-5057-4959-8ad8-fca96b9e80b5","slug":"architecture-minimalism","name":"Architecture Minimalism","summary":"Loopflow stays legible and smaller as it evolves. Public APIs, durable data, process boundaries, and control authority map to intentional product concepts and one owner. Repository-wide reduction removes obsolete paths and duplicated truth; code, CLI, DTO","definition":"Loopflow stays legible and smaller as it evolves. Public APIs, durable data, process boundaries, and control authority map to intentional product concepts and one owner. Repository-wide reduction removes obsolete paths and duplicated truth; code, CLI, DTOs, user documentation, and the architecture map describe the same supported system. Changes preserve active work, human decisions, and historical evidence.","flows":{"first":null,"loop":null,"finally":null},"krs":[{"text":"At chapter review, every public, durable, and cross-process concept in the reviewed repository has one intentional owner and truth source, with no unexplained duplicate authority or obsolete active path. The repository is simpler in named, reviewable ways than the chapter baseline, and implementation, CLI, DTOs, user documentation, and architecture map agree at the same revision. Four actual weekly checks judge the same reviewed source locally and in the hosted environment and retain their scope, findings, and coverage limits; reconstructed receipts do not replace missing observations. Every changed execution or placement path passes its recorded preservation and authority counterexamples.","holds":false}]},"runtime":{"work_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-08-22T01:16:11Z","iteration":119,"pending_observations":0,"provider":"codex","last_failure":{"message":"project runner failed: Project plan refresh blocked before the next phase: could not refresh wave/infrastructure from Linear: Stored linear token expired and automatic refresh failed: linear OAuth refresh failed: the token endpoint rejected or could not complete the request. Run `lf auth linear` once to reconnect.. Reconnect or run `lf pm sync --wave infrastructure`.. Project Work proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b did not continue on its stale plan; repair Linear planning, then restart it with `lf project run 62b73cde-5057-4959-8ad8-fca96b9e80b5`","occurred_at":"2026-08-28T22:01:04Z"}},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"tasks":[{"task":{"id":"e3f42e6a-885e-4d15-b7b5-bdccf68e00bd","identifier":"LOO-287","name":"Reduce competing concepts and align the reviewed architecture","description":"After the Task execution authority change and LOO-257, perform one coherent repository-wide reduction/documentation pass. Identify actual competing authorities or obsolete active paths, remove or simplify them, and make implementation, CLI, DTOs, user documentation, and the architecture map agree at the same reviewed revision. Resolve the retained local/hosted checker discrepancy by judging the identical reviewed source. Preserve active work, human decisions, exact control authority, and historical evidence. The finite checker covers only declared categories; a green bounded checker or vocabulary/line-count deletion alone does not establish A1. Retain four actual weekly observations with scope, findings, and coverage limits; missing observations are not reconstructed. Do not create one Task per historical remainder.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Queued behind the opening authority change and LOO-257; select earlier only for a demonstrated blocker or competing authority in those proofs. No execution launch or publication occurs as part of creating this planning record.","rank":0,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-287/reduce-competing-concepts-and-align-the-reviewed-architecture","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188166Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"a30ea5c3-028c-41a6-93eb-5a8a285f4c01","identifier":"LOO-286","name":"Finish Task-owned Flow execution with one authority and lossless cutover","description":"The outcome is a bounded Task worker owning immutable current execution; generic helper Runs remain available, and Wave/Project judgments remain finite attributed operations. Typed delivery and planning operations retain their own authority. Helpers may perform independently authorized edits and delivery operations; Task attribution itself does not authorize cursor movement, terminal transitions, or process signals.\n\nThe Task must reconcile the revised design with every retained counterexample:\n\n* A stale child cannot rewrite replacement human state or perform preparation side effects before establishing its authority.\n* Migration preserves controller-only autonomous progress and reconciles stale position rows before removing their old owner.\n* Missing executable definitions remain explicitly non-executable; ordinary retry or old human approval cannot erase an explicit-restart requirement.\n* Wave startup cannot silently replace historical execution or discard queued work.\n* An exact human decision has a functioning public continuation path, with settlement and launch outcomes reported separately.\n* Policy changes cannot overwrite concurrent intent or silently replace an active invocation. Historical Project execution has an explicit preservation and disposition path when live Project execution is removed.\n\nCompletion also requires the previously absent real provider death/replacement proof, helper-versus-worker authority proof, and configured CLI/Home/app path evidence. A killed `sleep`, passing store CAS, account-preflight failure, or app-shaped fixture is narrower evidence and must be labeled accordingly. App closure and optional service shutdown must not corrupt execution or become prerequisites for Task operation.\n\nKeep these as one coherent authority change with internal slices, following the branch’s current design. The retained review’s deferred generic advancement receipts are not automatically requirements for the revised Task-only model; their intended observable guarantees must survive.\n\nFinal human execution-model decision — 2026-09-23: Wave, Project, and Task all remain durable Work. Long-lived implementation pursuit and PR ownership belong to Tasks; Wave and Project operations are bounded Runs against their durable records.\n\nExisting implementation: /Users/jack/src/loopflow.wave-agents, branch jack-heart/wave-agents. Current complete PM snapshots and focused Work projections contain no Task association for that branch; lf task status wave-agents reports no Task exists. This issue tracks the existing change. Preserve that checkout, branch, research, reviews, and existing writer. Do not prepare another checkout, start a second writer, or restart the work merely because this tracking issue now exists. Reconcile its serial PR association through existing owners before launching a Task worker.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Opening Architecture allocation for the existing implementation; no controller launch authorized by this planning operation. No execution launch or publication occurs as part of creating this planning record.","rank":1,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-286/finish-task-owned-flow-execution-with-one-authority-and-lossless","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188167Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"2ada2b81-ffe1-40cb-9544-8c7bcb613c66","identifier":"LOO-257","name":"Base new Task worktrees on current canonical main","description":"## Outcome\n\n`lf task run` creates a new Task worktree from the exact current canonical-main commit even when that commit is ahead of or otherwise unpublished to origin. Placement records that commit as the Task/PR base and leaves publication/rebase to the normal Task lifecycle.\n\n## Observed configured failure — 2026-08-21\n\nThe Product Wave committed durable memory on canonical main. Starting LOO-256 then failed before Task creation because main was ahead of origin/main. The refusal made the Wave’s own durable learning prevent all subsequent Task work.\n\n## Proof\n\n* In a temporary repository whose clean canonical main is one or more commits ahead of origin/main, `lf task run` creates the sibling Task worktree and bases it at the exact local canonical-main HEAD.\n* No push, reset, force-push, origin equality check, allowlist, or manual reconciliation is required.\n* Existing Task/worktree reuse remains idempotent.\n* Landing still rebases/integrates through normal Loopflow PR mechanics.\n* A newly authorized configured Task can be created from clean, unpublished canonical main without first publishing Wave commits; do not reopen completed LOO-256.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nThis intentionally supersedes LOO-175’s fixed fetched-origin placement precondition while preserving its minimal-PR-range outcome. Remove the fixed-context precondition rather than extend it. Do not silently include uncommitted filesystem changes, mutate origin, or weaken Task/worktree ownership.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: rewrite. Allocation: queued. Move to Architecture Minimalism; preserve technical contract, replace obsolete LOO-256 demo target. Select earlier if placement blocks selected work.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":3,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-257/base-new-task-worktrees-on-current-canonical-main","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188168Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"d4af661c-669f-4fc7-88d9-dea5005f275f","identifier":"LOO-270","name":"Make architecture drift evidence consistent across local and hosted trees","description":"Outcome: scripts/check_architecture.py judges the reviewed repository identically in a clean hosted checkout and a normal Loopflow checkout containing ignored runtime archives. Current counterexample on 2026-08-23: all 167 discovered boundaries map, but the local check fails only on stale vocabulary inside ignored .lf/prompts and .lf/tmp artifacts that hosted CI never sees. Contract: exclude non-reviewed generated/runtime material by one principled source-of-truth boundary, not a growing stale-term or path allowlist; preserve coverage of reviewed .lf configuration and every existing architecture category. Proof: focused tests create ignored runtime artifacts containing retired vocabulary and remain green, while equivalent tracked/reviewed vocabulary still fails; the real local check and hosted workflow use the same behavior.","rank":2,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-270/make-architecture-drift-evidence-consistent-across-local-and-hosted","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188168Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"15ea26b7-0b66-4c79-94c1-a846bef80b1a","identifier":"LOO-253","name":"Main agents move off canonical main into a worktree","description":"PRINCIPLE: a main agent (one that runs on the canonical checkout, not a Task body) must not do work directly on main — it moves into a worktree. Two subjects, shipped in ONE diff sharing a worktree-move core:\n\nSUBJECT 1 — the WAVE agent (resident). Runs the wave loop with cwd = canonical main, so memory curation commits onto local main, drifting it ahead of origin/main and jamming Task placement. Fix: run the resident from a dedicated worktree; commit curation there; reach main via a CI-gated PR; canonical becomes read-only to the resident. This half is fully parent-reviewed — see scratch/main-agent-in-worktree.md on branch jack-heart/main-agent-in-worktree. (Project agent is a likely third subject; keep the core general enough to cover it.)\n\nSUBJECT 2 — default `lf`. The user's main/only agent interface when they run bare `lf` in a repo. Meet them in whatever context (plain repo, on main, in a worktree) and don't refuse; as soon as real work happens on main, transparently MOVE to a worktree and carry the in-flight work along. Scoped to bare/default `lf` — `lf code` and other specialized subcommands keep their assumptions and do NOT get the auto-move.\n\nNOT the fix: branch-identity verification, ownership-collision guards, wt-remove warnings — that hardens the model in the wrong direction. The move is accept-the-context, then relocate off main.\n\nAbsorbs cd07e2e2 (the default-lf framing).","rank":4,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-253/main-agents-move-off-canonical-main-into-a-worktree","workspace":{"slug":"main-agents-move-off-canonical","branch":"jack-heart/main-agents-move-off-canonical","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.main-agents-move-off-canonical"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_2c822e334dc7498e92734ed21d736764","project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","routing_project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-22T01:15:00Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-253 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.main-agents-move-off-canonical is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-253`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.18819Z","evidence_age_secs":2818689,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-253 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.main-agents-move-off-canonical is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-253`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_7fab8abc2e9d42a2a9a855cb403dfe97","sequence":1,"slug":"main-agents-move-off-canonical","branch":"jack-heart/main-agents-move-off-canonical","base_commit":"d854d79561e9115458d4a895e4d5c38dd433e1dd","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-21T22:47:15Z","presentation":{"title":"Main agents move off canonical main into a worktree — agents: isolate default and wave sessions in worktrees","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-253](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-253/main-agents-move-off-canonical-main-into-a-worktree)\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\n# From the canonical default branch\nlf\nlf wave product\ngit worktree list\n```\n\nBare `lf` reports the sibling worktree it moved into. Wave residents run from a stable `<repo>.wave-product` worktree, while canonical main remains clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoves default terminal agents and long-running Wave residents out of the canonical checkout. This prevents agent activity from dirtying the shared control plane while preserving existing local commits, tracked edits, and untracked files instead of refusing the session or discarding work.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Carries canonical-main state into an author-scoped agent worktree and resets main to the fetched default branch; deliberate non-default checkouts and existing linked worktrees remain unchanged\n- Gives each Wave resident a deterministic sibling worktree, with collision-safe names for nested Waves\n- Loads canonical skills and flow definitions while reading mutable `GOAL.md`, `MEMORY.md`, and cron state from the resident checkout\n- Restricts inline resident writes to the Wave's own goal and memory, then commits them and opens a strict CI-gated pull request\n- Blocks Wave relocation while resident changes are dirty, unpublished, or under an open PR, and syncs merged state back to canonical main before moving files\n- Adds behavioral coverage and updates the repository and Wave ownership documentation","head_sha":"4b178c0d6d2a5065164153a75c4593d6eddeb06f"},"github":{"number":1230,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1230"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-22T00:52:51Z","head_sha":"4b178c0d6d2a5065164153a75c4593d6eddeb06f","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"2c8d4177d19163237ac54dcbfeb7bc154c660d78","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"cd07e2e2-65c0-43f3-ae59-859c634e7859","identifier":"LOO-254","name":"[absorbed into 15ea26b7] Default lf: accept context, move to worktree","description":"Vision: a new user runs `lf` inside their repo and that IS their main/only agent interface. That agent may itself choose to run a Wave or Project agent directly. Default lf should meet the user in whatever context it finds — plain repo, sitting on main, or already in a worktree — and NOT refuse.\n\nLoosening intake is coupled with absorbing the user into the workflows that work best. Keystone behavior: as soon as possible, notice we are doing real work directly on the canonical/main checkout and transparently MOVE to a worktree — create or switch into one and carry the in-flight work along. Permissive intake + automatic promotion into the good pattern, rather than (a) rejecting the context or (b) letting work dirty main.\n\nSCOPE — this belongs to bare/default `lf` specifically (the empty invocation that is the user's main agent door). Specialized subcommands do NOT get the auto-move: `lf code` and friends can keep assuming they're in a worktree and just work outside one too. Don't make this a global CLI policy; it's the behavior of the default entrypoint.\n\nThis unifies two problems that are the same problem:\n\n* The wave resident dirtying canonical main (task 15ea26b7) is a special case of 'work is happening on main; move to a worktree.'\n* A user/agent running default lf on main and starting real work should be lifted into a worktree early and quietly.\n\nToday the machinery hardens against these contexts instead:\n\n* 'Wave and Project turns require the canonical main checkout' — refuses.\n* `lf task run` refuses a pre-existing un-owned worktree/branch — refuses.\n  Both are the wrong reflex: refuse-the-context instead of accept-then-move.\n\nDo NOT fix this by adding branch-identity verification, ownership guards, or wt-remove warnings — that hardens the model in the wrong direction.\n\nExplore, don't over-specify: the concrete surface — what counts as 'real work on main', when exactly to move, how the move carries uncommitted/committed state, how the default agent decides to escalate — is for design to work out.","rank":5,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-254/absorbed-into-15ea26b7-default-lf-accept-context-move-to-worktree","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.18832Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"prs":[],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"28836de1-0ac0-46da-981e-5961efe225ed","identifier":"LOO-73","name":"Make Project planning changes take effect without restarting or stranding work","description":"Outcome: A human can change a Project definition or KRs in Linear and active Project Work adopts the authoritative plan at a safe boundary without losing direction, observations, or identity. If adoption is unsafe, status says exactly why a restart is required; it never continues silently on stale planning. Contract: the Project seed carries the complete PM definition and KR set, including more than four KRs; one authoritative representation owns the plan; refresh occurs at a bounded phase boundary; removal or archival produces a truthful state rather than a crash or stale loop. Proof: tests start Project Work with five or more KRs, edit the definition and KR set while it is active, and show the next bounded turn receives the exact new plan once while prior direction and evidence remain intact.","rank":6,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-73/make-project-planning-changes-take-effect-without-restarting-or","workspace":{"slug":"make-project-planning-changes-take","branch":"jack-heart/make-project-planning-changes-take","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-project-planning-changes-take"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_316fe0299ce9402ebce76f1c021b0e77","project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","routing_project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-22T20:46:30Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-73 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-project-planning-changes-take is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-73`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188342Z","evidence_age_secs":5426799,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-73 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-project-planning-changes-take is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-73`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_6160a9890ab3424a9bdf2a76d7a519e4","sequence":1,"slug":"make-project-planning-changes-take","branch":"jack-heart/make-project-planning-changes-take","base_commit":"90b89225c240b84fc77d40a2ec99c2d8b3b3acae","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-22T20:30:49Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1184,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1184"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T20:30:53Z","head_sha":"de2f2846b8132c7fdc0ac14fc9ee892d80ef19d3","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"f704fa0a9445c1443d1eb51640a26f7faba812df","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"0194b0da-1465-471a-9fed-a0c470f89851","identifier":"LOO-208","name":"Make Loopflow architecture explainable from one map","description":"Outcome: A maintainer can start at one top-down map and understand the durable control owners, truth sources, process boundaries, public APIs, and provider edges that explain Loopflow. The implementation and vocabulary follow that map instead of preserving alternate historical models. Contract: name each core real-world concept once; link it to its authoritative data structure and public surface; identify persistence and process ownership; name allowed historical-only vocabulary; add a bounded drift check that finds unnamed owners, mirrors, shims, and stale pre-Run, pre-Home, or pre-native-PM language. Proof: every landed change for four consecutive weekly checks maps to an existing concept or updates the map in the same change, and each check reports zero unexplained owner, mirror, or shim.","rank":7,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-208/make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from-one-map","workspace":{"slug":"make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from","branch":"jack-heart/make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_4995e07e047b4898870cebaaa2bd1c8f","project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","routing_project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T20:27:59Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-208 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-208`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188488Z","evidence_age_secs":5514310,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-208 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-208`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_6d6e7f9f83664655b137dfe63127cde0","sequence":1,"slug":"make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from","branch":"jack-heart/make-loopflow-architecture-explainable-from","base_commit":"b5d23f9562e33b1500874559fd822aab39aee38c","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T19:31:45Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1159,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1159"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-21T20:14:29Z","head_sha":"2212a2ce8d5b0a1c83bc6b9ebe2553d0263c2935","after_merge":"complete_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":"649121be5435926ae44a398fd4ba3e21fb44d5c5","abandoned_at":null}],"active_pr":null},{"task":{"id":"52beae61-e799-455c-b8dc-25548d259457","identifier":"LOO-127","name":"Let every repository own and safely move its Waves","description":"Outcome: Independent repositories can use the same Wave names without cross-repository attachment, and an existing Wave can be renamed or rehomed without losing its identity or history. Contract: Wave resolution is scoped by canonical repository plus slug; ambiguous bare-name lookup fails closed; rename and rehome preserve the Wave UUID, PM binding, Work and Run history, journal, and authored paths; stale repository paths are repaired transactionally. Proof: deterministic tests register, launch, query, and display an Infrastructure Wave in two repositories, exercise rename and rehome, and prove neither repository can resolve or mutate the other Wave.","rank":8,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-127/let-every-repository-own-and-safely-move-its-waves","workspace":{"slug":"let-every-repository-own-and","branch":"jack-heart/let-every-repository-own-and","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-every-repository-own-and"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_2e1035726a794330a182d564b908327e","project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","routing_project_id":"proj_b98a997ce55a45d1981ad9537d21da3b","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-22T19:53:13Z","provider":"codex"},"direction":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-127 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-every-repository-own-and is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-127`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T16:13:09.188647Z","evidence_age_secs":5429996,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-127 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-every-repository-own-and is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-127`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"prs":[{"id":"pr_8ad9290b8e5f4a51ba6486e5371da3b0","sequence":1,"slug":"let-every-repository-own-and","branch":"jack-heart/let-every-repository-own-and","base_commit":"553a6e3806a56e9c31c6cb94566de5aad352bf42","phase":"merged","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-21T22:26:33Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1169,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1169"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-07-22T18:11:09Z","head_sha":"72d7ec54244b21a3f8a3663d6a7b951d2f63b795","